Let me summarize what I think your setup looks like: you have a (flat) LAN
with a 3000 and a PWS. The LAN connects to the outside world by means of a
gateway (I translate that to a router).
You wrote that the 3000 gets its names resolved then the gateway itself is
properly configured. The route to the DNS server is OK and the return path
as well. If that is all true then the PWS must have a problem somewhere.
Like an improper mask or a default route not set or improperly set. What
happens when the PWS pings the external DNS server? Or better still, a
traceroute to the DNS server?
Or possibly, the gateway does NAPT and all inbound TCP/ and UDP/IP traffic
on port 53 is sent to the 3000.

Hans



